      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Location, Location, Location!\n\nBarry Murphy Auctioneers are delighted to present this beautifully appointed four-bedroom detached residence, ideally positioned in the picturesque village of Crooke, Passage East, Co. Waterford.\n\nOccupying an impressive circa 0.3-acre site, this unique home enjoys an enviable position overlooking The Suir Estuary, with uninterrupted panoramic views across the estuary towards Creadan Head,Arthurstown, Duncannon and the Hook Lighthouse Peninsula Co. Wexford. Offering a wonderful balance of contemporary comfort, generous accommodation and an exceptional coastal setting, this is a home that truly makes the most of its surroundings with newly renovated pedestrian access to Passage Beach located a stones throw from the property, ideal for those who enjoy sea swimming. Crooke is renowned for its scenic beauty, relaxed village atmosphere and strong sense of community. The local GAA club is within easy walking distance, while the property is ideally positioned just 10km from Waterford City Centre and approximately 8.5km from the Ardkeen area and UHW, and 1.7km from the Passage East car ferry making it an excellent choice for commuters and families seeking a peaceful coastal lifestyle without compromising on convenience.\n\nCrooke occupies a particularly special position on the western shore of Waterford Harbour, with sweeping views across the estuary towards County Wexford. Woodstown Beach is just 3.5km away, offering a beautiful setting for walking, swimming and enjoying the coastline. The nearby villages of Faithlegg, Cheekpoint and Dunmore East further enhance the appeal, providing an array of leisure facilities, amenities and coastal attractions.\n\nThe thoughtfully designed split-level accommodation extends to approximately 175sq m and is arranged to maximise both space and natural light. The ground floor comprises an impressive entrance hall, living room and fourth bedroom with en-suite.\n\nThe lower level features a superb open-plan kitchen/dining area, a useful utility room, guest WC and a comfortable sitting room with French doors opening directly onto the deck, creating a seamless connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces and making the most of the spectacular outlook.\n\nUpstairs, the three bedrooms all enjoy sea views, including a spacious master bedroom with en-suite, together with two further well-appointed bedrooms and a family bathroom. The elevated position of the bedrooms allows the stunning coastal outlook to be enjoyed from multiple rooms throughout the home.\n\nExternally, the property truly comes into its own. The south-facing rear garden, laid in lawn with a generous decked area, enjoys spectacular views across the Suir Estuary towards Arthurstown and Duncannon. This exceptional outdoor space provides an idyllic setting for al fresco dining, entertaining family and friends, or simply relaxing while taking in the ever-changing views across the harbour.\n\nFurther features include double-glazed windows, oil-fired central heating and mains water.\n\nThis is a rare opportunity to acquire a distinctive family home in an outstanding coastal setting, combining exceptional views, generous accommodation and convenient access to Waterford City.\n\nViewings are highly recommended and can be arranged through Sole Agents Barry Murphy Auctioneers. \n\nGround Floor\nEntrance Hall: 4.26m x 4.52m. Tiled floor. \nBedroom 4: 3.12m x 3.12m. Wood floor, blinds. \nEn-suite: 3.13m x 0.88m. Wood floor, WC, wash hand basin, electric shower, blinds. \nLiving Room: 3.43m x 3.77m. Wood floor. \nLower Level\nKitchen/Diner: 4.31m x 8.43m. Tiled floor, cream fitted kitchen with integrated dishwasher & fridge, island, bay window with window seat, French doors to garden, under stairs storage 2.7m x 0.8m. \nSitting Room: 5.30m x 4.10m. Wood floor, open fireplace, French doors to deck.\nUtility Room: 1.6m x 2.76m. Tiled floor, fitted units, plumbed for washing machine. \nWC: 1.6m x 0.86m. Tiled floor, WC, wash hand basin. \nSitting Room: 5.38m x 4.1m. Wood floor, fireplace with open fire, French doors to deck and garden. \nFirst Floor \nLanding: 0.92m x 5.56m. Carpet. \nMaster Bedroom: 5.33m x 4.11m. Wood floor, fitted wardrobes. \nEn-suite: 3.16m x 1.14m. Fully tiled, Velux, WC, wash hand basin, electric shower. \nBedroom 2: 3.18m x 3.63m. Wood floor, blinds, fitted wardrobe. \nBedroom 3: 3.24m x 3.33m. Wood fooor, bliss, fitted wardrobe. \nBathroom: 2.61m x 3.45m. Fully tiled, Wc, wash hand basin, corner bath. \nHP: 1.75m x 1m."
      },
